# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Restart `npm run dev` after editing —
# Vite inlines these at build time, so a running dev server will not pick up a change.
#
# ─── PUBLIC_ IS NOT A MISTAKE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This site is fully static, so there is no server to keep a secret in. Every value
# here is inlined into the JS bundle and visible to anyone who views source. Only
# put values here that are safe in public. Never add a real secret — an SMTP
# password, an API key that can spend money, a Turnstile *secret* key. Those go in
# the Web3Forms dashboard, which is a server.

# Web3Forms access key — the destination for all four contact forms.
# Get one free at https://web3forms.com: enter dylannagel05@gmail.com, confirm the
# email, and paste the key it gives you here. Without it, the forms render an
# honest "delivery is not configured" state and send nothing.
#
# This key is a routing identifier, not a credential: it means "deliver to this
# inbox" and cannot read past submissions or change the destination. It can be
# scraped and POSTed to by a bot, which is what the honeypot and (once configured)
# Turnstile are for. See src/lib/contact.ts.
PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
